  "data": {
    "document": "Core Rules",
    "section": "18. Transports",
    "ruleNumber": "18.02",
    "summary": "Once battle round one has begun, your unit can board your **TRANSPORT** after it makes a **fall-back move**, an **advance** or a **normal** move. Bring every model to within 3 inches of it and check **all** the other requirements. The **TRANSPORT** needs unused **[transport capacity](vsdata:core-rule/transport-capacity)** for the entire unit, and its datasheet must list the unit as **eligible to embark**. Any unit placed on the board earlier that turn is barred. If the unit boards, the active player takes it off the board and it is now embarked. The able to embark check uses this rule’s conditions as modified by any other applicable rule.",
